AIM: To implement Network Address Translation (NAT) to translate private IP addresses into public IP addresses.
Example:
Private IP	Public IP
10.10.10.2	50.50.50.2
10.10.10.3	50.50.50.3
20.20.20.2	60.60.60.2

3. Topology
Devices: - 2 Routers PT: R0 and R1- 2 Switches PT- 2 PCs: PC0 and PC1 - 1 Server: Server0
Connections:
- PC0 and Server0 connect to Switch0.
- Switch0 connects to R0.
- R0 connects to R1 using Serial2/0.
- R1 connects to Switch1.
- Switch1 connects to PC1.
Use automatic connection in Packet Tracer, as specified in your journal.

4. IP Configuration
DIRECT CONFIGURE
| Device  | Interface    | IP Address    | Subnet Mask       |
|---------|--------------|---------------|-------------------|
| R0      | Fa0/0        | 10.10.10.1    | 255.255.255.0     |
| R0      | Serial2/0    | 192.162.10.1  | 255.255.255.0     |
| R1      | Fa0/0        | 20.20.20.1    | 255.255.255.0     |
| R1      | Serial2/0    | 192.162.10.2  | 255.255.255.0     |
| PC0     | FastEthernet | 10.10.10.2    | 255.255.255.0     |
| Server0 | FastEthernet | 10.10.10.3    | 255.255.255.0     |
| PC1     | FastEthernet | 20.20.20.2    | 255.255.255.0     |

Default gateways:
- PC0 and Server0: 10.10.10.1 - PC1: 20.20.20.1

R0:
Configure Static NAT:
ip nat inside source static 10.10.10.2 50.50.50.2
ip nat inside source static 10.10.10.3 50.50.50.3
interface fa0/0
ip nat inside
exit
interface serial2/0
ip nat outside
exit
Configure static route R0:
ip route 60.0.0.0 255.0.0.0 192.162.10.2
end

R1
Configure Static NAT:
ip nat inside source static 20.20.20.2 60.60.60.2
interface fa0/0
ip nat inside
exit
interface serial2/0
ip nat outside
exit
Configure static route R1:
ip route 50.0.0.0 255.0.0.0 192.162.10.1
end


6. Verification - On both routers, check the routing table:
show ip route
Check NAT translations:
show ip nat translations

From PC0, test the public IP of PC1:
ping 60.60.60.2
From PC1, test the public IP of PC0:
ping 50.50.50.2
